.TH yes "" "Command"
.SH NAME
yes \- print infinitely many responses
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fByes [\fIanswer\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
yes -- print infinitely many responses
Usage:	yes [ answer ]
The default 'answer' is 'y'.
.HE
.B yes
repeatedly prints
.I answer
(default:
.BR y )
followed by a newline, forever, until it is killed or its standard
output is closed.
It takes at most one argument.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B yes
prints
.B "Usage: yes [answer]"
and exits with status 1 if given more than one argument.
